---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const total = (await getCollection('concepts')).length;
---

<Base title="How to use · NH-Learnway" total={total}>
  <main>
    <a href="/" class="back">← All concepts</a>
    <div class="eyebrow">The whole thing is free</div>
    <h1>How to use this</h1>

    <p class="intro">
      Each dot is one concept. Open it, read the sections slowly, and only move on once you
      can say in your own words why it exists and what it is good and bad at.
    </p>

    <h3>For each concept</h3>
    <p>
      Read it. Do the one tiny build. Then solve the two problems on LeetCode. That loop —
      <b>understand, then build, then practice</b> — is the whole method.
    </p>

    <h3>The free path</h3>
    <p>
      You never pay. Use the free <b>NeetCode 150</b> list and its <b>YouTube</b> videos to
      know what to practice and to get unstuck, and solve the problems on <b>LeetCode's free
      tier</b>. If anything on NeetCode's site is locked behind Pro, that same problem is free
      on LeetCode. Skip Pro.
    </p>

    <h3>When to move on</h3>
    <div class="rule">
      Don't move on because you finished reading. Move on when you can explain the concept
      from memory, build something small with it, solve several problems without looking at
      solutions, and recognize when it applies.
    </div>

    <h3>The one rule</h3>
    <div class="rule">
      Understanding is the goal, not filling this in. Learn the concept first, then mark it.
      If a week passes where you read a lot and solved nothing, that is the trap — go solve
      one problem.
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    main { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 18px 100px; }
    .back { text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; }
    .back:hover { color: var(--ink); }
    .eyebrow { margin-top: 18px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--mint); text-transform: uppercase; }
    h1 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 30px; margin: 5px 0 16px; color: var(--ink); }
    .intro { font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); background: var(--night-2); border: 1px solid var(--line-dim); border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 16px; }
    h3 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 17px; margin: 26px 0 8px; color: var(--ink); }
    p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
    p b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
    .rule { background: var(--night-2); border: 1px solid var(--line-dim); border-radius: 12px; padding: 13px 15px; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); }
  </style>
</Base>
